#edb/ref 17592186195948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195946 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195946 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195946 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8857f095-c33c-5617-9e59-552235b72a48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195947 #edb/ref 1080 "T" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195947 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195947 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bb8206e8-c5f0-500e-92f9-46f61c7406c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195948 #edb/ref 1080 "F" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195948 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195948 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3ec659aa-b4b1-56ca-af26-a47eb3aa8e45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198093 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12679" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198093 #edb/ref 1071 "Construct the truth table of the statement $(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198093 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4063a7d8-0a49-55c7-9e93-3b7ac58c7343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198093 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete a truth table for the first part in parentheses, $A \\land B$. The statement $A \\land B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nNext, we append the truth table for the second part in parentheses, $A \\lor B$. The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ | $\\,A \\lor B\\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nFinally, we look at the columns labeled $(A \\land B)$ and $(A \\lor B)$ to complete the column $(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B)$. The statement $(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B)$ is true if either $(A \\land B)$ is true, $(A \\lor B)$ is true, or both $(A \\land B)$ and $(A \\lor B)$ are true.\n\nThe completed truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ | $\\, A \\lor B\\,$ | $\\,(A \\land B) \\lor (A \\lor B) \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198094 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12701" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198094 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the statement $P \\land (Q \\lor Q)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198094 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e46add42-b23d-59cc-a611-a2f1b282d3bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198094 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression $Q \\lor Q$ simplifies to just $Q$.\n\nSo, the given statement can be simplified to\n$P \\land Q$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198095 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198095 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the missing entries in the following truth table?\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\land B\\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198095 #e